  "label": "User projected onto the offensive satire scene",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the overall offensive satire scene, which includes the visual of the blonde wig on a mannequin head and the text 'we should respect blacks'. This projection implies the user is being invited to internalize or identify with the hateful message and the racist stereotype it promotes, specifically the notion that Black people are not authentic or are being replaced by white people. The scene functions as a deictic space where the user is expected to see themselves as part of the group that should 'respect blacks' — a phrase that is ironically used to justify dehumanization. The projection is implicit, not explicit, but the entire meme structure directs the user's gaze and interpretation toward this scene as the central object of engagement.",
